The agent's name (vision M10 §10, slice P1): the dashboard tells the chat
header and the tabs what the agent is called, and the first run asks.

The name is the Name line of the agent's IDENTITY.md, one of the personality
files upstream's gateway already serves (`GET/PUT /api/personality/IDENTITY.md
?agent=<alias>`) and the Runtime reads into every prompt, so the model and the
pages agree without a new field. The overlay holds the logic (`lib/identity.
logic.ts`), the client (`lib/identity.ts`), the cache and hook (`lib/agentName.
tsx`), the first run's name screen (`pages/setup/Setup.tsx`), the Looks page's
Name card and the Home tile; this patch touches the upstream files only where
the alias was shown as the agent's name: the chat header (AgentChat.tsx), the
tabs and the agent picker (ChatTabBar.tsx), the strings (i18n.ts), and the
test list (package.json).

